   {
    "id": "01a0e196-7f0e-7795-a731-4ca6bab82a04",
    "conversation": "01a0e196-188d-7331-8e18-d07e4bde12a2",
    "sequence": 4,
    "role": "val",
    "content": "My lord, I have no volume on obstetric procedures in the House\u2019s record. A cesarean section is a surgical operation performed to deliver a fetus by incising the mother's abdomen and uterus. The incision allows the baby to be withdrawn directly from the womb, bypassing the vaginal canal. It is employed when a natural birth would pose significant risk to mother or child, such as fetal distress, malpresentation, placenta previa, or maternal health complications. The procedure requires anesthesia and careful post\u2011operative care to ensure recovery for both mother and infant.",
    "created": "1790491131.662"
   },
